    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the values of \\( y \\) for which the expression \\(\\frac{y+6}{y^2-5y+4}\\) is undefined, we need to identify the values of \\( y \\) that make the denominator zero, because division by zero is undefined.\n\nFirst, set the denominator equal to zero and solve for \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny^2 - 5y + 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, factor the quadratic equation:\n\\[\ny^2 - 5y + 4 = (y - 1)(y - 4) = 0\n\\]\n\nNow, set each factor equal to zero to find the values of \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny - 1 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y = 1\n\\]\n\\[\ny - 4 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y = 4\n\\]\n\nThese values of \\( y \\) make the denominator zero and thus make the expression undefined. Therefore, the expression is undefined for \\( y = 1 \\) and \\( y = 4 \\).\n\nTo find the sum of all these values, we add them together:\n\\[\n1 + 4 = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of all values of \\( y \\) for which the expression is undefined is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
